WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.920
The gloriously Chilling Adventures of Sabrina
has arrived on Netflix in a devilishly dark

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.160
take on the popular teenage witch who so many
loved watching in her mid-1990s sitcom.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.019
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm diving into the ten biggest

00:00:15.019 --> 00:00:18.871
differences between Chilling Adventures of
Sabrina and Melissa Joan Hart's Sabrina The

00:00:18.871 --> 00:00:20.260
Teenage Witch!

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.680
Keep watching to the end to find out the Riverdale
cameo you won't want to miss!

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.820
And if you're finding me for the first time,
every week I do deep dives into your favourite

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.820
TV shows and movies, so tap the bell to stay
up-to-date with all my new videos.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.530
One of the highlights of the 90s sitcom was
Sabrina's cat, Salem.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:41.920
The show brought the wisecracking kitty to
life using a mix of animatronic puppets and

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:47.219
real cats, while his frequent sarcastic comments
were memorably voiced by Nick Bakay.

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:51.550
In the show, Salem was previously a warlock
but had been turned into a cat to punish him

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:55.489
for attempting to take over the world, not
that that stopped him from getting up to all

00:00:55.489 --> 00:01:00.030
kinds of other mischief to much comic effect
in keeping with the show's generally light

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.030
tone.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:04.220
As for the Chilling Adventures of Sabrina,
if you were hoping for some black cat back-chat,

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:08.830
then you're out of luck, as this particular
feline version of Salem never speaks.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:13.180
Except to briefly introduce himself the first
time he turns up at Sabrina's home, but that's

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.020
when he's in his goblin form.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.020
"Sabrina!"

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.900
"I heard you calling in the woods."

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:25.170
"And I came.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.600
Meow!"

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:32.160
The new Salem arrives after the half-witch
tries summoning a familiar, and despite not

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:36.400
having the gift of the gab, he still gets
an active part and some cool scenes, and is

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.780
a rather adorable presence.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:43.270
A non-verbal Salem doesn't mean you'll miss
out on the kind of snark and comedic dialogue

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:48.120
you enjoyed in the 90s show though because
another character takes on a similar role.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:52.200
Sabrina's cousin Ambrose is a charming, witty
warlock who didn't appear in the original

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.530
sitcom but is based on a character from the
comics with his TV backstory being given a

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:59.450
tweak from the Chilling Adventures of Sabrina
books.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:04.710
Like sitcom Salem, TV Ambrose has been punished
for his part in a conspiracy; in Ambrose's

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.869
case, he tried to blow up the Vatican.

00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:11.501
In the new series, Ambrose, who's brilliantly
played by Chance Perdomo, is someone who Sabrina

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:17.590
often turns to for advice and help as a partner-in-crime
in her various schemes, much like sitcom Salem.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:22.580
As for Sabrina's aunts, Hilda and Zelda, there's
a similar dynamic between the sisters, the

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:26.960
big difference being that the 90s show has
a lighter, fairy godmother-style, fluffier

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:32.330
version, while the Netflix series takes things
to a much darker, devil-worshipping place.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:37.290
In Sabrina the Teenage Witch, Zelda is the
intelligent, science-minded, logical aunt;

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:41.330
while Hilda tends to be less practical, and
generally more fun-loving and outgoing.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:45.540
They get up to stuff like making "perfect"
men out of dough and turning themselves into

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:49.350
teenagers so they can keep their eye on their
niece at a gig without her knowing.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:53.540
In the Chilling Adventures, Zelda is played
by Australian actress Miranda Otto of Lord

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:59.330
of the Rings fame and is very much a no-nonsense
witch and certainly the much sterner of Sabrina's

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.330
aunts.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:04.980
Zelda's mid-Atlantic accent and whole manner
positively oozes Bette Davis, which is funny

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:10.200
because Kiernan Shipka who plays Sabrina recently
played Bette Davis's daughter in the TV series

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.200
Feud!

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.640
Aunt Hilda, meanwhile, has a British accent
and is a softer, more openly kind-hearted

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.780
witch, with a fun sense of humour and generally
less confidence than her sister.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:24.210
She's played by Lucy Davis, who you'll doubtless
recognise as Wonder Woman's Etta Candy.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:28.170
The on-screen chemistry between Miranda Otto
and Lucy Davis is fantastic and they take

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:33.090
the bickering between the aunts on the 90s
show to a whole new, Cain and Abel level of

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.090
darkness!

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:37.650
In the first season of Chilling Adventures,
we're told that Brina's parents have died

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.650
in an accident.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:42.660
Her mother was mortal and her father Edward
was a progressive High Priest in the Church

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:43.660
of Night.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.290
That's a huge difference from the original
90s show where Sabrina's parents are both

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.330
still alive though they're divorced.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:53.430
In the sitcom, Sabrina's father lives in her
spell-book, where she sees him early on in

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:56.680
the first season, though she does later get
to see him in real life too.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:01.570
As for Sabrina's mortal mother, well, her
half-witch daughter isn't allowed to see her

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:05.560
as if she does her mother will turn into a
literal ball of wax, and that's something

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.180
that did actually happen on the show!

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:12.560
When it comes to their tone and look, Sabrina
the Teenage Witch and the Chilling Adventures

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.060
of Sabrina are absolutely poles apart.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:21.230
Sabrina the Teenage Witch ran for seven seasons
from 1996 and was a brightly coloured and

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.660
lit situation comedy.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:27.600
It was full of goofy storylines, cartoony
characters, and zany schemes with all sorts

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.410
of weird and wonderful magic goings-on including
episodes that featured Sabrina's boyfriend

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:38.150
turning into a frog, her seriously OTT pancake
addiction, and the time she almost had to

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:39.480
marry a troll.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:43.970
Things were generally kept bright and breezy
and didn't have to make sense over the seasons

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:48.160
with characters sometimes disappearing with
no real explanation, like Sabrina's best friend

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.000
Jenny after Season One.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.630
In comparison, Chilling Adventures is much
more devilish, far darker, and definitely

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:56.870
more intense and gory.

00:04:56.870 --> 00:05:02.010
Season 1 of the slow-burn show follows Sabrina's
"dark education", and really leans into its

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:06.190
horror origins, with loads of easter eggs
and references to classic fright flicks.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:11.541
In some nice meta-moments, the Netflix show
tips its hat to its 90s predecessor, with

00:05:11.541 --> 00:05:16.720
Zelda asking to be saved "from the melodramatics
of a teenage witch", and Prudence noting that

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.460
Sabrina "has gone dark"
So, overall, Chilling Adventures is more akin

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:25.260
to Buffy the Vampire Slayer, while Sabrina
the Teenage Witch is more like the 60s sitcom

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:26.260
Bewitched!

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:30.990
Now, while the original live-action TV show
was set in Westbridge, Boston, and had Sabrina

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:35.200
only discovering that she was a half-witch
on her 16th birthday; Netflix's series is

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:39.851
located in Greendale, across the Sweetwater
River from Riverdale, and Sabrina knows she's

00:05:39.851 --> 00:05:43.210
a half-witch, half-mortal right from the start.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:48.330
Time-wise, Sabrina the Teenage Witch was very
much set in the era it was made, the mid-1990s

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.330
onwards.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:53.980
But when it comes to the Chilling Adventures
of Sabrina, it's impossible to pin down exactly

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.840
when this new show is set.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:06:00.840
That's because the series is a deliberate
mix of many different eras, so modern sensibilities

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:05.140
and adult themes are blended with costumes,
sets, and props drawn from Victorian times

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:08.920
to the 1960s, 70s, 80s and beyond.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:13.389
Another big difference between the Netflix
series and the mid-90s show is that over its

00:06:13.389 --> 00:06:17.560
seven-season run, Sabrina the Teenage Witch
welcomed a huge number of celebrities on set

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.660
in cameos and guest star roles.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:25.870
Among the very many famous faces was a pre-Breaking
Bad Bryan Cranston who played a magical lawyer,

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:30.210
Mary Poppins star Dick Van Dyke who was an
old friend of Salem's, actress Raquel Welch

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:34.620
who was Sabrina's Aunt Vesta, magicians Penn
and Teller who played the Head of the Witches

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:39.450
Council and his assistant, and a ton of music
stars including Britney Spears, Coolio, the

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:42.490
Backstreet Boys, and Usher who played a Love
Doctor.

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:47.170
But what this season of Chilling Adventures
of Sabrina does have is a Riverdale cameo!

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:51.890
Look out for Ms Wardwell ordering a pizza
because when the delivery boy arrives he turns

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.860
out to be Riverdale's Ben Button!

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:58.570
This isn't Ben's first time in Greendale as
he had music lessons and hook-ups at Miss

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.070
Grundy's home there.

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:04.990
But, spoiler ahead for Episode 2, Season 3
of Riverdale, Ben jumped out of a hospital

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:09.530
window after telling Betty and Jughead that
he was following the Gargoyle King's plan!

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:13.510
So, what are your theories about how Ben turned
up in the new Sabrina show?

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:16.700
And which other Riverdale characters would
you like to see appear in Season 2?

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:20.400
Now, I'd love to know if you're a fan of the
original Sabrina sitcom.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.420
And what do you think of the new show?

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.090
Let's continue the conversation in the comments
below!

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.300
And you can also follow me on Twitter.

